            <ArticleTitle>A case of successful laparoscopic resection of adrenal gland endometriosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2015.e7-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.fertnstert.2008.01.006</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To present a case of successful laparoscopic resection of adrenal endometriosis.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DESIGN" NlmCategory="METHODS">Case report.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="SETTING" NlmCategory="METHODS">University Hospital.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="PATIENT(S)" NlmCategory="METHODS">Forty-eight-year-old woman with left-sided abdominal and flank pain.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="INTERVENTION(S)" NlmCategory="METHODS">Laparoscopic radical adrenalectomy.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MAIN OUTCOME MEASURE(S)" NlmCategory="METHODS">Diagnosis and surgical approach to adrenal endometriosis.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULT(S)" NlmCategory="RESULTS">There have been two case reports of adrenal endometriosis. Based on a search of Medline and Google for &quot;adrenal endometriosis,&quot; this is the first known successful laparoscopic resection of adrenal endometriosis.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION(S)" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">We report the first case of successful laparoscopic adrenalectomy for the treatment of endometriosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
